{
  "_comment": [
    "Tier-1 standard-package family table for the dubIS->OpenPnP bridge",
    "(Phase 3a, first increment). Keyed on '<part_type>_<size_code>' where",
    "part_type is one of resistor/capacitor/inductor/led/diode and size_code",
    "is a standard imperial chip size (0201/0402/0603/0805/1206).",
    "",
    "body_width_mm / body_height_mm are the standard IPC/EIA land-pattern",
    "body dimensions for the chip size and are identical across families of",
    "the same size (the physical package footprint is size-defined, not",
    "type-defined).",
    "",
    "default_height_mm is a REASONABLE DEFAULT per (type, size) — NOT a",
    "measured value for any specific part. It is used only when dubIS has no",
    "part-specific height in its own spec data (see spec_extractor.py); real",
    "component height varies by manufacturer/construction (e.g. MLCC",
    "dielectric build-up, chip-inductor core height) and should be corrected",
    "per-part once dubIS has a real height source (Tier-2 / manual override).",
    "",
    "kicad_footprint follows the standard KiCad library naming convention",
    "'<Imperial>_<Metric>Metric' from the official *_SMD footprint libraries.",
    "openpnp_package is the corresponding OpenPnP packages.xml package id",
    "convention (<PREFIX><size>, e.g. R0402)."
  ],
